RF.put("questb:b45",{"8525":{"id":8525,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Rainbow Fin Albacore!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 rainbow fin albacore to Slicky Gastronome at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Rainbow Fin Albacore","desc":"What! You again? Well I'll be a monkey's uncle... except that I'm a gnome. Slicky Gastronome to be precise! So you're back to help out again eh? Well, I can't say as I blame you. Don't you just love the smell of all of that food? <drool>\nEnough loitering! Get out there and bring me back more rainbow fin albacore!","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"What! You again? Well I'll be a monkey's uncle... except that I'm a gnome. Slicky Gastronome to be precise! So you're back to help out again, eh? Well, I can't say as I blame you. Don't you just love the smell of all of that food? <drool>\nEnough loitering! Get out there and bring me back more rainbow fin albacore!","done":"I knew that you had it in you, kid. You've got the look of someone who knows what she likes. Specifically that you like pleasing me and the powers that be. And that you have, I guarantee.\nHaha, ok, I'll just get these fish properly stashed away, and then you and I can have a little talk concerning you collecting another twenty albacore.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.3,"n":"Slicky Gastronome","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8605":{"id":8605,"t":"The Horde Needs More Wool Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Wool Bandages to Healer Longrunner at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Wool Bandage","desc":"Good to see you again, ‹class›. We are still working on preparations here for the war effort, and I can still use all of the help that you can give in gathering up wool bandaging. Any assistance at all will be greatly appreciated. I only hope that our efforts will be good enough. I've lost too many noble souls on the battlefields of yesterday to not do everything in my power to see to it that doesn't happen again.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"You are an honorable ‹class›, ‹name›! I will see to it that these bandages get into the right hands. You have my thanks, and that of the Horde.\nGo in peace, and return to me again should you find yourself with excess wool bandaging. We can use all of the help that we can get here.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.1,"y":74.2,"n":"Healer Longrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"525":{"id":525,"t":"Further Mysteries","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Decrypted Letter to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\nDecrypted Letter\nProvided: Decrypted Letter","desc":"I decrypted the letter, but I don't know what to make of it. You found this among thieves in the Alterac foothills? Very strange...\nYou should take this to the magistrate of Southshore. Although this letter is cryptic, his is the closest town to Alterac; if a threat is brewing, then he should know.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›. Have you been traveling through the foothills and mountains again? What news do you bring?","done":"<Maleb reads the letter.>\nThis is translated from a letter you found in a Syndicate encampment? This was not written by a thief, or even a noble of Alterac.\nIt appears The Syndicate has ties to another power, and I shudder to think what that might be.\nDun Morogh Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.1,"y":59.1,"n":"Magistrate Henry Maleb","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"7165":{"id":7165,"t":"Earned Reverence","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Insignia Rank 3","desc":"I must know, ‹name›. When you look directly into the eyes of the enemy, do you see fear? Do they now cower in your presence? They must realize that they are defeated!\nYou have earned reverence among the Guard.\nPresent your insignia!","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostwolf Insignia Rank 4\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"So many slain. Blood drenches the fields. Yet... You live... You have persevered. You have led our armies to many victories. For this, then, soldier, you have earned a new rank.\nPresent your insignia.","done":"<Warmaster Laggrond roars.>\nThey have already begun telling tales of your deeds, soldier. The Stormpike shakes in fear when your name is uttered. Carry on!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"685":{"id":685,"t":"Wanted!  Otto and Falconcrest","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Wanted! Otto and Falconcrest. New rewards: Arathi Armbands.","obj":"Bring Otto's Head and Falconcrest's Head to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\nOtto's Head Otto\nFalconcrest's Head Lord Falconcrest","desc":"The Stromgarde Militia has placed bounties on the heads of Lord Falconcrest, and his bodyguard Otto. Falconcrest heads the Syndicate's efforts in the Arathi Highlands, and his death would cause a major disruption in those efforts.\nHis bodyguard Otto, although not a strategic target, is a fierce opponent and has killed dozens of our defenders.\nTheir bounties may be collected from Captain Nials.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRod of Sorrow War Rider Bracers Arathi Armbands\nNew in Forever: Arathi Armbands.\nExperience: 3,900\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello. Do you have a report to submit?","done":"Falconcrest and Otto? Wonderful!\nHere is your reward, ‹name›. I am happy to pay it.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46,"y":47.8,"n":"Wanted Board","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Captain Nials","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1085":{"id":1085,"t":"On Guard in Stonetalon","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Gaxim.","desc":"The situation here in Stonetalon is obviously grave for a night elf and gnome to be working together.\nThe Venture Co. has devastated these lands and I've spent most of my time putting an end to the destruction.\nDo not judge Gaxim prematurely; he understands the need for us to work together.\nIf you wish to aid us, then start by speaking to Gaxim.\nI'm sorry I cannot send you back to Tara with good news yet. Perhaps soon.","rew":"Experience: 170\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"Treacherous...treacherous and dangerous, that's what this land is.\nBut I'm here to show the night elves that it's a little safer with the help of good ole engineering and a dash of magic.\nSee, swearing off magic completely won't help the night elves -- they need it. The world needs it. And with engineering and alchemy to boot, you can't go wrong. The possibilities are endless.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.9,"y":66.8,"n":"Kaela Shadowspear","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3565":{"id":3565,"t":"Xylem's Payment to Jediga","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Xylem's Note to Jediga in Azshara.\nXylem's Note\nProvided: Xylem's Note","desc":"What is it? Oh yes, your payment. Of course.\nTake this and be off with you. I'm sure Jediga is awaiting oh so patiently for your return.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,800","back":"Well, what did Xylem have to say? He didn't do anything to you, did he? Cast a spell on you? Con you into doing work for him?","done":"No problems? None at all? Well, that's something to be said... I expected him to show some sort of reluctance or to at least betray our deal. Hmm, maybe he can be trusted after all.\nWell, no need to dwell on it that much. Here's your share. Thank you for your help.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4765":{"id":4765,"t":"Delivery to Ridgewell","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ridgewell's Crate to Remington Ridgewell in Stormwind.\nRidgewell's Crate\nProvided: Ridgewell's Crate","desc":"I have packaged Doomriggers Clasp into a crate, suitable for shipment to Stormwind. ‹name›, you have been extremely helpful -- can I ask you for one last favor?\nDeliver the crate to Count Remington Ridgewell. You will find him in the Keep of Stormwind. I am sure he'll be very pleased to see what you have for him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwiftfoot Treads Blinkstrike Armguards\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I was told a messenger would come. One with a gift from Blackrock Spire.\nAre you he?","done":"Ah, so you are he! You have my thanks, ‹name›. And... if you didn't already know... the gratitude of a noble in the house of Ridgewell is nigh worth a king's ransom.\nBurning Steppes Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Mayara Brightwing","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Count Remington Ridgewell","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2765":{"id":2765,"t":"Expert Blacksmith!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Claim your reward from Galvan the Ancient!","desc":"When you first came to me, I knew that you would turn out to be one of my finest pupils! It was without hesitancy that you gave up a trinket of some power to McGavan. You did this only so that you could meet me. Such blind faith and devotion to the craft should be rewarded.\nYou have attained expertise over blacksmithing, ‹name›. Reap the rewards!","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet of Expertise\nExperience: 3,900","done":"It is only fitting that you receive a trinket of far greater power than the one you sacrificed to get here. Use it in good health, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"96045":{"id":96045,"t":"Camping 101 alchemy","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Vosur Brakthel in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your alchemy skill to 20","desc":"Now that you've taken up Alchemy, I can also teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp once you've learned a bit. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":66.4,"y":55.2,"n":"Vosur Brakthel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"98285":{"id":98285,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Speak with the Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"An engineer is ever-resourceful, and if you are in the wilds alone, it's always good to be able to put your trade to use. No good camp is complete without a few helpful constructs!\nYes, come back and see me when you've gained a little bit of experience as an engineer and I can show you how to make something special!","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":54,"y":39,"n":"Strange Hermit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"97965":{"id":97965,"t":"Camping 101 first aid","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Naleeia Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your first aid skill to 20","desc":"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a ‹class›.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43,"y":46.2,"n":"Naleeia Tattermend","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96605":{"id":96605,"t":"The great outdoors","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sit near Kaga's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.\nUse the /sit emote near the campfire\nGain the Boosted Rest buff","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","back":"Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.","done":"So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94285":{"id":94285,"t":"Craftsmans writ unstable trigger","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Unstable Trigger\nUnstable Trigger","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Unstable Trigger, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Unstable Trigger Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94285","cats":["crafting"]},"7885":{"id":7885,"t":"Armor Kits","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"8 Rugged Armor Kit Larion 10 % , Rabid Blisterpaw 0 % , Scorching Elemental 0 %","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"You might not realize this, but running a traveling carnival is costly! Everything wears down so fast it's a wonder we can turn a profit.\nBecause of all those hidden costs, we're always looking for ways to maintain our equipment as cheaply as possible. Our tents, for instance, tear regularly but I've found that leather armor kits make great patches. Can you find and bring me some armor kits? That'll save us a bundle! Do that, and I have a fistful of Darkmoon Faire tickets for you...","done":"Great! This will work great! I just noticed a rip in a tent over yonder, and one of these armor kits is just what I need to patch it up!\nThank you very much, ‹name›. These armor kits will save us a ton in repair costs. Here are your tickets - you deserve them!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.6,"y":70.8,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.2,"y":42.5,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"7485":{"id":7485,"t":"Libram of Protection","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 54 instead of 58.","obj":"Bring a Libram of Protection, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 2 Large Brilliant Shards, and 1 Frayed Abomination Stitching to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Protection.\nLibram of Protection Prince Tortheldrin 2 % , Magister Kalendris 2 % , Illyanna Ravenoak 2 % , Tendris Warpwood 2 % and 4 more\nPristine Black Diamond Veteran Commando 2.3 % , Witherbark Speaker 1 % in Zul'Gurub , Winterax Axe Thrower 1 % , Lady Illucia Barov 1 % in Scholomance and 4 more\n2 Large Brilliant Shard\nFrayed Abomination Stitching Ramstein the Gorger , Venom Belcher 15 % in Stratholme , Bile Spewer 15 % in Stratholme , Patchwork Horror 15 % in Stratholme","desc":"He wept like an infant at the loss of this libram. Mind you, I myself have wept over texts - there is no greater loss than that of knowledge and history - but to cry over this nearly useless jumbling of incantations? Preposterous! It left me to believe that the Prince was doing him a favor in flaying the flesh from his bones.\nBring the Libram along with a pristine black diamond, large brilliant shards, and a frayed abomination stitching and I shall recreate the Arcanum.\nOh, and check the north wing.","rew":"You will receive:\nArcanum of Protection\nExperience: 1,650\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"My patience prevents your suffering.","done":"Yes, yes... Calm yourself. As promised, here is your Arcanum.\nStart Lorekeeper Lydros End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7485","cats":["dire-maul"]},"6125":{"id":6125,"t":"Power over Poison","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.","desc":"You've learned what it means to cure poison without the benefit of spiritual aid. Remember what others must endure in fighting poisonous afflictions as you soon embrace your newfound power over poison.\nYou should now return to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus, ‹name›. He, no doubt, has a very important spell to teach you now that the student understands the lesson given unto him/her.\nFarewell, young druid. We shall speak again.","rew":"You will learn: Cure Poison\nExperience: 975\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Welcome back - I've been following your progress on this lesson since you left, and I must admit I was surprised to learn about the situation in Auberdine. This does bear some further investigation, as the introduction of such poisons into the environment is most upsetting to the balance.\nYou handled yourself with grace under pressure. For that, I can find no better way to reward you than with permanent power over poison. Use it well, ‹name›... use it well.\nMoonglade Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"9165":{"id":9165,"t":"Writ of Safe Passage","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the signed Writ of Safe Passage to Dispatch Commander Metz at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nWrit of Safe Passage\nWrit of Safe Passage Signed\nProvided: Writ of Safe Passage","desc":"Without the help of adventurers, my caravan would have never made it! Scourge were coming out of the woodwork to try and stop us from getting here.\n<Guard Didier wipes his brow.>\nNow we need to wait here for Field Marshal Chambers to arrive. He'll sign your writ of safe passage to take back to Dispatch Commander Metz at Light's Hope Chapel.\nAnd ‹name›, watch what you say around Chambers. He's the 'bite off your head and spit down your wind pipe' type of guy - except that he'll actually do it...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Dawn Insignia of the Crusade\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Name, rank and serial number!","done":"<Dispatch Commander Metz takes the writ and signs it.>\nExcellent work, ‹name›. Outstanding even! Take this as a token of our appreciation. No pun intended, scrub.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":48,"n":"Dispatch Commander Metz","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5805":{"id":5805,"t":"Welcome!","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Northshire Gift Voucher to Merissa Stilwell.\nNorthshire Gift Voucher\nProvided: Northshire Gift Voucher","desc":"Welcome to the World of Warcraft!\nAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Merissa Stilwell in Northshire Valley. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.\nThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDiablo Stone Panda Collar Zergling Leash","back":"Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!\nI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.","done":"You are indeed a special hero, ‹name›. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.4,"y":41.9,"n":"Merissa Stilwell","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"45":{"id":45,"t":"Discover Rolf's Fate","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the murloc village for Rolf, or signs of his death.","desc":"Upon further searching the area, you find webbed footprints leading east along the shore of Stone Cairn Lake. In the distance to the east, you can just barely see a Murloc village.\nPerhaps Rolf's fate ended there...","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"You find around the neck of the corpse a metal medallion inscribed with the words \"Footman Rolf Hartford.\"","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":72.7,"y":60.3,"n":"A half-eaten body","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":79.8,"y":55.5,"n":"Rolf's corpse","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"91725":{"id":91725,"t":"Stolen enchanting supplies","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 5 Stolen Enchanting Supplies from gnoll camps around Stone Cairn Lake, then return to Blixie Fitzwink near the Tower of Azora.\n5 Stolen Enchanting Supplies","desc":"I was sent by Master Theocritus to pick up some enchanting supplies from the trading post, but on the way back I was ambushed by a pack of gnolls!\nI dropped the package and escaped, but if I return without it, I'll be cleaning up after the polymorph experiments for weeks as punishment! Do you think you could find the supplies for me?","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find the supplies?","done":"Oh, that's a relief! It looks like it's all here. Thank you!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":63.2,"y":72.6,"n":"Blixie Fitzwink","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3645":{"id":3645,"t":"Membership Card Renewal","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -2g instead of 0.","rew":"You will receive:\nGnome Engineer Membership Card","back":"In order to renew your membership card, you will need to pay the renewal fee of two gold pieces.","done":"Since you're a practitioner of Gnomish engineering and are in good standing, I am able to renew a lapsed membership card for the fee of two gold pieces. Once this fee is paid, you will be reissued a new membership card. This will allow access to Gnomish engineering schemata from appropriate trainers.\nThis card will last for two weeks of activity, at the end of which your membership fees will become due again! If you want to access schemata, you'll need to bring your dues out of arrears.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4445":{"id":4445,"t":"Corrupted Whipper Root","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a whipper root plant. The visible roots of the plant appear tough and leathery, and a slimy film hangs from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 3 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Whipper Root. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":40.7,"y":19.1,"n":"Corrupted Whipper Root","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5165":{"id":5165,"t":"Dousing the Flames of Protection","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Purified Moon Well Water, douse the flames of the four braziers of protection within Shadow Hold in Felwood, then return to Greta Mosshoof in the Emerald Sanctuary.\nExtinguish the Brazier of Pain\nExtinguish the Brazier of Malice\nExtinguish the Brazier of Suffering\nExtinguish the Brazier of Hatred\nProvided: Purified Moonwell Water","desc":"Now, you must return to Jaedenar. The braziers are more than likely spread throughout Shadow Hold. Douse each of their flames and the protections the Council has set up will fall for at least a short period of time. I will be waiting for that to happen. When it does, I will look deep within the Hold and try to find out who the head of this beast is. Then, and only then, will we see about attacking them directly.","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"The braziers must be extinguished if we are to have any hope of being prepared for a much greater battle. Going in to the dragon's lair without any knowledge is a fool's errand. And this is much worse than a dragon. The Shadow Council are solely responsible for a great number of crimes and atrocities. We'll have to work quickly if we're to stop them.","done":"I was able to see you with my spells as soon as the last brazier's flames died. Well done, ‹name›.\nI learned a few things before the Shadow Council's warlocks were able to recast their spells. Hopefully it will be enough.\nFor now, rest. I will tell you what I've learned in a moment.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.2,"y":82.1,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5885":{"id":5885,"t":"Salve via Skinning","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Patch of Tainted Skin","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!\nWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.","done":"This is exactly what I need. Here - take these plant salves and use them to reclaim Felwood from the corruption. We must persevere, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4125":{"id":4125,"t":"The Missing Courier","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate the courier's boat somewhere along the coast of Feralas.","desc":"It's been about a week since Raschal, the courier, set out for Thalanaar. He knows Feralas well; he's been with us since General Feathermoon led the expeditionary forces here. I know his plan was to take a row boat down the coast and try and traverse across southern Feralas to avoid the Horde camp.\nI couldn't find his boat, but maybe you can. Maybe it is hidden, or maybe it was sunk. Regardless, it might hold a clue as to where he is. If you uncover something, please let me know.","rew":"Experience: 2,700\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"You have found what appears to be a wrecked row boat. Through the slightly muddy water you see gaping holes riddling the port side; the boat is nearly shredded down to its simple wooden frame. Whatever broke this boat most likely tried to snap it in two. A small crest of the Feathermoon Stronghold is painted on the starboard side.\nIn the mud at the base of the boat, a glint of something metallic catches your eye...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":45.4,"y":65,"n":"Wrecked Row Boat","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2845":{"id":2845,"t":"Wandering Shay","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Pick up Shay's Bell from the chest.\nEscort Shay Leafrunner to Rockbiter's camp.\nShay's Bell Shay's Chest","desc":"Do you think you could help me find my way back to my friend, Rockbiter? He was supposed to be watching me... But I do have a tendency to wander off now and then. There are just so many things to see, and I get so distracted.\nThere is one thing that will always work to get my attention, though.\nInside this chest, you'll find a bell that is very precious to me. I just love the sound of it. You have my word, if I wander off, all you have to do is ring it and I'll come running back.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGranite Grips Vinehedge Cinch\nExperience: 4,550","back":"I was gettin' worried 'bout ya! Thank you so much for bringin' Shay home, ‹name›.","done":"What? You say dis bell will work when Shay runs off? Well, how 'bout that!\nSince you did so much fer me, here ya go, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":38.2,"y":10.3,"n":"Shay Leafrunner","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":42.4,"y":22,"n":"Rockbiter","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7725":{"id":7725,"t":"Again With the Zapped Giants","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker to zap any kind of giant found in Feralas into a more manageable form. Bring 10 Miniaturization Residues found on the zapped versions of these giants to Zorbin Fandazzle at the docks of the Forgotten Coast, Feralas.\n10 Miniaturization Residue Zapped Cliff Giant , Zapped Wave Strider , Zapped Land Walker , Zapped Shore Strider and 1 more\nProvided: Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker","desc":"I know you've gathered residue for me already... but should you find yourself for want of an encore performance to a fun-time activity, I can always use more residue.\nWhile I can't offer nearly as much in the way of compensation again, I'll be more than happy to spread the good word of your service to all my goblin friends with ears.\nBelieve me sir/madam when I say that these goblins have quite large ears.","rew":"Money: 21 0 gold, 21 silver, 0 copper Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"Ah, the fruits of research and utilization in the form of sweet, sweet residue. Well, that is to say, I don't taste it or anything when I study it.\nMuch.","done":"Inconceivably fantastical, ‹name›! You've come through for me again, and for that I thank you.\nThank you!\nWhile you may find this coin to be a little less than you're accustomed to, rest assured your great deeds on the field of goblindom are echoing through the halls of power in the Steamwheedle Cartel. Should you need something else to do, then by all means talk to me!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":44.8,"y":43.4,"n":"Zorbin Fandazzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2925":{"id":2925,"t":"Klockmort's Essentials","lv":30,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.","desc":"A gnome friend, Klockmort Spannerspan, sent word to me from Ironforge. He tells me he needs help on a dangerous, but essential, mission into Gnomeregan, the once great gnome city now contaminated and filled with mad gnomes and their devices.\nI must stay here, but my heart aches to help my friend. If you can go in my stead, then I would be much indebted to you.\nYou may find Klockmort in Tinkertown, in Ironforge.","rew":"Experience: 250\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"I do! I do need help with a mission into Gnomeregan. And you're just the ‹class› to do it!\nDarnassus Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":59.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Mathiel","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62,"y":28.5,"n":"Klockmort Spannerspan","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"4605":{"id":4605,"t":"The Sparklematic 5200!","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSparklematic-Wrapped Box\nExperience: 2,450","done":"As quickly as it started, the Sparklematic 5200 comes to an abrupt halt. A simple \"ding\" is heard from the machine, and the mouth of the machine spirals upward. Inside the Sparklematic 5200 is a small box wrapped in a little bow. The machine would appear to wrap an object up after eliminating its grime-encrusted status. Even if the machine didn't work, at least the item is now wrapped in a pretty box.\nWell, there is one way to find out if it cleaned the item or not...\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4605\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200! this quest\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"9085":{"id":9085,"t":"Shadows of Doom","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 55.","obj":"Go to a summoning circle and kill a Shadow of Doom, then return to Commander Thomas Helleran at Light's Hope Chapel in Eastern Plaguelands.\nShadow of Doom slain","desc":"After you bring down the defenses of the Scourge summoning circles that have appeared in the zones under attack, you will be able to confront the acolytes who protect them.\nIn truth, these are not men. They are shadows, some of the Lich King's most frightening creatures. They can be revealed using the necrotic runes they carry, and then destroyed with magic or strength of arms.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Blessed Wizard Oil 5 Consecrated Sharpening Stone\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Have you had any luck, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Commander Thomas Helleran","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"7805":{"id":7805,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":26.2,"n":"Mistina Steelshield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"9005":{"id":9005,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Dreadmist Mask and Dreadmist Robe.\nDreadmist Mask Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nDreadmist Robe General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Mask Deathmist Robe\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Dreadmist pieces in exchange for your new Deathmist Mask and Robe?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8685":{"id":8685,"t":"Mistwalker the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":62.6,"y":31,"n":"Elder Mistwalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9325":{"id":9325,"t":"Stealing Thunder Bluff's Flame","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 70s instead of 0. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,000, 0.99 times as much. New rewards: Fiery Festival Brew. No longer rewards Toasted Smorc, Midsummer Sausage, Fire-toasted Bun, Elderberry Pie.","obj":"Return the Flame of Thunder Bluff to the Festival Loremaster.\nFlame of Thunder Bluff\nProvided: Flame of Thunder Bluff","desc":"This flame, stolen from the shaman of Thunder Bluff, floods you with warmth. This raw power is foreign to you, but the Loremaster might know more...","rew":"New in Forever: Fiery Festival Brew.\nYou will receive:\n20 Fiery Festival Brew 20 Burning Blossom\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,950","back":"You're practically glowing, ‹race›. What do you have there?","done":"Unless I miss my guess, this fire has been taken from the cliffs of Thunder Bluff! How it sings with the power of the spirits! You are quite the thief, ‹name›. Take this as just payment for your skill. Now, if only we had the flames of all three cities...\nTeldrassil Dun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.5,"y":92.2,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":25.1,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50,"y":72,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"6845":{"id":6845,"t":"Uncovering Past Secrets","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.","desc":"Anyway, you should check back with me relatively soon... that is if you want to know what was in here. As soon as I find out what it is, and if it's indeed a book, I'd be happy to share that information with you.\nIn the meantime, I'd check in with the den mother of this little bear camp, Rabine. No doubt he'll want to know what crazy antics you've been up to. Never leave the den mother waiting, ‹name›... that is, unless you want to be doused in honey.\nIt's happened, trust me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRing of Living Stone Glowing Crystal Ring\nMoney: 1 70 1 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,550\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Ah, ‹name› - I had hoped you would stop by. I am glad to see you well.\nI received notice you would be coming in from the field, and I wanted to personally express the Cenarion Circle's gratitude for the assistance you've given us thus far. No doubt there are more secrets to uncover from Silithus; your delivery to Umber should prove most interesting once uncovered. Please, accept this as a token of our continued appreciation for your aid.\nThank you, generous ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":44.9,"y":35.6,"n":"Umber","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":51.7,"y":45.1,"n":"Rabine Saturna","e":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"95805":{"id":95805,"t":"Grace of anshe and musha","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Carry the Smoldering Incense to the shrine of An'she and Mu'sha in the southeastern hills before the incense burns to ash in ten minutes!\nProvided: Pouch of Smoldering Incense","desc":"The sun and the moon, An'she and Mu'sha, are not part of our world like the elements, yet their light gives us life, guidance, and hope.\nWe pay respect to the spirits of the world, and so we pay respect to the twins as well.\nIf you would show your respect, take this smoldering incense and bring it to a shrine in the hills to the southeast, overlooking the mesa, south of the quilboar. Be quick, so that you can reach the shrine before the incense burns away.\nDon't get it wet!","rew":"You will receive:\nScorched Leather Pouch\nExperience: 180\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"<The smoke from the incense rises toward the sky.>","done":"<As you empty the incense into the fire, the scent wafts around you, leaving you with just the empty pouch and a subtle sense of fulfillment.>","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":42.6,"y":92,"n":"Seer Graytongue","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":56.6,"y":88.7,"n":"Ritual Fire","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"765":{"id":765,"t":"Supervisor Fizsprocket","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Supervisor Fizsprocket and return his clipboard to Morin Cloudstalker at Bloodhoof Village.\nFizsprocket's Clipboard Supervisor Fizsprocket","desc":"According to the documents you salvaged from the caravan, the Venture Co. created many plans to attempt to drive us from our lands here, so that they could have free reign to plunder our lands.\nThe depths that they would sink to accomplish their goals disgusts and appalls me. I want the mastermind behind their plans killed. His name is Supervisor Fizsprocket, you will find him at the Venture Co. mine east of the ravaged caravan. Bring me his clipboard, we shall see if we find out anything useful.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCompact Fighting Knife Goblin Smasher\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I seethe with anger at the thought of the atrocities the Venture Co. is willing to perpetrate against us in the name of profit.","done":"My anger is somewhat lessened at the news that the villain Fizsprocket is dead. I will go through his personal effects and see if there is any additional information about what the Venture Co. has planned for the future. Thank you for your efforts, ‹name›.\nMulgore The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":54.8,"y":64.3,"n":"Morin Cloudstalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9245":{"id":9245,"t":"Icy Scale Gauntlets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 16 Heavy Scorpid Scale, 5 Essence of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.\n5 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n16 Heavy Scorpid Scale\n5 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create Icy Scale gauntlets. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nIcy Scale Gauntlets","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1645":{"id":1645,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nTome of Divinity","done":"Here in Ironforge, I am responsible for putting paladins on the path to greater virtue as they devote themselves to the Light and defend Azeroth from the Scourge and other threats.\nThe time has come for you to take your first step towards being truly virtuous. If you accept it, I will give you a Book of Divinity. In studying it, you shall learn some about the Light, and what is expected of you. If you understand it, and are capable, then you will succeed in attaining greater abilities.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7645":{"id":7645,"t":"Manna-Enriched Horse Feed","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -50g instead of 0.","obj":"Retrieve 20 Enriched Manna Biscuits - the key ingredient in making Manna-Enriched Horse Feed - for Merideth Carlson at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. The Argent Dawn is known as the sole purveyor of the biscuits.\nYou also need to give her 50 gold to soothe her ruffled sensibilities.\n20 Enriched Manna Biscuit","desc":"The Silver Hand thought me MAD when I told them that I could make a special horse feed that could nourish spiritual horses. EVERYONE thought I was mad! Well, now it's payback time!\nI'll make what you need, PALADIN... so-called CHAMPION... but it will cost you. I need special biscuits - Enriched Manna Biscuits sold only by the Argent Dawn - for this blend. I also demand, yes DEMAND gold as compensation for the misery I have endured!\nShow me the sacrifice you tout so much, PALADIN.","rew":"You will receive:\nManna-Enriched Horse Feed\nExperience: 650","back":"Yes, I've proved you wrong now, haven't I? I've proved them all wrong! I WAS RIGHT ALL ALONG!!!","done":"YES, NOW WHO - wait - you're giving me the gold too? You weren't the one who called me mad (actually they called me a fruitcake nut-job)... still, you're willing to show sacrifice even for wrongs you've not committed?\nI... I misjudged you, ‹name›. Should you need more horse feed, come see me. I will give it to you free of charge. Thank you... noble ‹class›.\nI am going to keep the money though - I'm not that much of a nut-job as to give up a fortune.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":52.2,"y":55.5,"n":"Merideth Carlson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"3085":{"id":3085,"t":"Hallowed Tablet","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Hallowed Tablet and speak to Ken'jai outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.\nHallowed Tablet\nProvided: Hallowed Tablet","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the priest trainer Ken'jai. He would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"So ya made it... good good! Da spirits tol' me you be comin' to see Ken'jai soon enough. Let me be one o' da first to welcome ya to da Valley of Trials. Dis place not be your home fer long, but while it is, why dontcha make da best o' it.","done":"As ya test yeself, ya'll find ya have better an' better control o'er da spirits--ya'll be callin' on dem fer greata an' greata tings... dat's where ol' Ken'jai come in. You come talk to ole Ken'jai when ya feel yer ready. If da spirits agree, den we see 'bout teachin' ya more powerful abilities... but only if da spirits agree.\nGo now, talk to da rest of da Valley's people. Speak to me again later.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":68.8,"n":"Ken'jai","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5645":{"id":5645,"t":"A Lack of Fear","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from A Lack of Fear.","obj":"Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.","desc":"‹name›, your High Priest Rohan would have an audience with you in Ironforge. Make haste, my strong friend, your next test quickly approaches. Although I wish I could bear witness to your race's own special rites, my place is here. But may the Light go with you in your travels. Rohan should still be in the Mystic Ward once you reach the city. He will be waiting.","rew":"You will learn: Fear Ward\nExperience: 390","done":"You've got the makings of a great ‹class›, ‹name›. Keep up the good work!\nYou've already shown you're ready for battle. Perhaps it's time we taught ya a little somethin' more.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.1,"y":22.8,"n":"Toldren Deepiron","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5725":{"id":5725,"t":"The Power to Destroy...","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,950 experience instead of 1,450, 2.03 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring the books Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether to Varimathras in Undercity.\nSpells of Shadow Searing Blade Cultist 5 % , Searing Blade Warlock 5 %\nIncantations from the Nether Searing Blade Cultist 5 % , Searing Blade Warlock 5 %","desc":"Many denizens of the Legion bestow gifts on their followers as you may well know. Some of these gifts the Dark Lady feels would be better off in her hands than in the hands of those with... lesser vision.\nA sect of the Shadow Council hidden in caverns below Orgrimmar known as the Searing Blade are a prime example. The Lady tells me that members of the Searing Blade have come into the possession of two powerful spell books--she would like to \"borrow\" these books from them. You will get them for her.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGhastly Trousers Dredgemire Leggings Gargoyle Leggings\nExperience: 2,950\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"There are a hundred other tasks awaiting my attention, ‹class›. Do you have the books?","done":"Good, ‹class›. You have done well in serving the Dark Lady. Your continued perseverance and ambition will be of great use to the Lady's subjects. Return to me again in the future. Perhaps I will have other tasks for you that will aid the Dark Lady in her attempts at overtaking the Lich King and completely freeing the Scourge.\nUndercity Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ragefire-chasm"]},"125":{"id":125,"t":"The Lost Tools","lv":16,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Foreman Oslow of Lakeshire wants you to retrieve his toolbox from the bottom of Lake Everstill.\nOslow's Toolbox Sunken Chest","desc":"I could really use a hand here, ‹name›. With the town under siege, it's been hard to get supplies. My tools were being delivered from Goldshire by wagon but the bridge was blown out. We put the tools in a boat but the orcs hit it with a catapult. Just my luck, my toolbox sank right to the bottom of the lake.\nRetrieve my toolbox, ‹name›, and I'll make it worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Medium Armor Kit\nExperience: 875\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Were you able to find my tools?","done":"Excellent recovery, ‹name›! I never thought I'd see these tools again.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":27.1,"y":48.6,"n":"Foreman Oslow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8845":{"id":8845,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with the Darkspear tribe. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":46.3,"y":35.1,"n":"Officer Vu'Shalay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"1885":{"id":1885,"t":"Mennet Carkad","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.","desc":"‹name›? Not quite what I was expecting, considering Carkad himself has taken an interest to you. Looks can be deceiving though, right?\nEither way, you should go see him as soon as possible. You wouldn't want to know what happened to the last few that chose to ignore his summons.","rew":"Experience: 210","done":"Hm. No doubt you made your way here at first mention of my summons, yes? Of course. I would expect no less from a prospective Deathstalker.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.8,"y":52,"n":"Marion Call","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2205":{"id":2205,"t":"Seek out SI: 7","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Keryn Sylvius's package to Master Mathias Shaw at the Stormwind Barracks.\nDelivery to Mathias\nProvided: Delivery to Mathias","desc":"The badge? Oh, it's nothing, fish - nothing you could handle anyhow. By the looks of you, I'd say Mathias is likely to mistake you for the cheese delivery boy/girl instead of a proper rogue. Regardless, I've been assigned a job and I've made a promise to deliver on that job.\nSpeaking of which, deliver this package to Mathias and he may give you a small task or two.\nGet cracking.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 0 silver, 85 copper Experience: 210","back":"Can I help you, ‹class›?","done":"You found me - and by looking at you, I'd say the run and subsequent search may have been a great strain on your system, both mentally and physically.\nWould you like Renzik to show you the way to an inn or are you ready for some work?\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.9,"y":65.9,"n":"Keryn Sylvius","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"97245":{"id":97245,"t":"Call of fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the home of Kuramaa in the Shen'dar Highlands, and defeat the spirit in combat. Bring Kuramaa's Mask to Olariaan Swiftburn in the Gustberry Lowlands when you are victorious.\nKuramaa's Mask","desc":"The residents of the Shen'dar Highlands speak of an ancient forest sprite called Kuramaa. They say it lives inside of a twisted stump at the summit of a hill near the highlands Anchor Pylon.\nGo to the highlands and find this stump. Rap your fist upon the bark and Kuramaa will appear. Best the spirit in combat, and bring me its wooden mask.\nBe warned however, this entity will be exceptionally resistant to much of your magic. Only the touch of flame will lay low the spirit.","back":"The spirit of Kuramaa is eternal, and it will manifest again when it is needed. It's mask is a source of great power, and will prove invaluable to the ritual we must complete.","done":"We now have what we need. We will light the eternal flame and commune with the spirits of fire.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":51.2,"y":86,"n":"Olariaan Swiftburn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8285":{"id":8285,"t":"The Deserter","lv":59,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the restored tablet to Hermit Ortell in Silithus.\nRestored Twilight Tablet\nProvided: Restored Twilight Tablet","desc":"There are rumors of a Twilight's Hammer member called Ortell having deserted his sect. Word has it he hid in the mountains south of Southwind Village, where he lives as a hermit. Perhaps you can enlist his help in deciphering the tablet.\nTake the restored tablet with you and seek out Ortell.","rew":"Experience: 4,800\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle\n0 reputation with Leatherworking - Tribal","back":"You! How did you find me? Who are you? You weren't followed, were you? Speak!","done":"I see you're familiar with my old organization. You must be with Cenarion Hold.\nYou seek information to use against them? Come closer, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":67.2,"y":69.8,"n":"Hermit Ortell","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"1005":{"id":1005,"t":"What lurks beyond","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Level 20 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 16 18 23 27 Side Both factions Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 1005","cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"95885":{"id":95885,"t":"The offering of blood","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Tortured Soul to give an offering of blood at the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril.\nWillingly offer blood\nRelease Tortured Soul\nTortured Soul slain","desc":"<All that's left now is the offering of blood.\nThe note scrap mentioned a 'willing sacrifice.'\nAn intense sense of dread washes over you.>","rew":"You will receive:\nLoop of Sacrifice\nExperience: 1,850","back":"<The offering stone is ominously still.>","done":"<The offering stone is inert now. It appears your ritual drained it of power. To what end, you do not know, but it is over now.\nThe rough stone cracks and crumbles, now devoid of purpose.\nSomething glitters from within the remnants...>","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":58.1,"y":69.9,"n":"Offering Stone","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"925":{"id":925,"t":"Cairne's Hoofprint","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Thunder Bluff to see about getting Cairne Bloodhoof's hoofprint for your ward.\nCairne's Hoofprint","desc":"They say that Cairne Bloodhoof is one of the greatest heroes the Horde has ever seen. When I grow up, I wanna be a hero of the Horde too!\nDo you know Cairne, ‹name›? Could you do me a favor, please? Could you get his hoofprint for me? I dunno how to ask him, and he'd probably be too busy for someone like me... but you! You're an adventurer just like he is! I bet he'd give you his hoofprint easy!\nPlease?","rew":"Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Horde","back":"When the orcs were alone and without friends, the tauren welcomed them to a strange land and shared with them without asking anything in return. That's honor, ‹name›.","done":"WOW! You got Cairne's hoofprint for me! Thank you very much! And wow... he wrote a personal message on here - to me! I knew he'd be totally cool, I just did! Maybe someday I'll thank him myself... when I become a hero of the Horde!\nYou're the best, ‹name›. Thank you for being so nice to me.\nStart Orcish Orphan End Orcish Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Horde Shareable No Quest ID 925\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 2,300 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Cairne's Hoofprint this quest\nTravel to Thunder Bluff to see about getting Cairne Bloodhoof's hoofprint for your ward.\nOrcish Orphan\n650 XP\n2 [ 60 ] A Warden of the Horde\nReturn your ward to the Orgrimmar orphanage by handing in the Orcish Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Battlewail in the Valley of Honor.\nOrcish Orphan\n1,650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1245":{"id":1245,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":30,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Defias Docket to Elling Trias in Stormwind.\nDefias Docket Defias Strongbox\nProvided: Defias Docket","desc":"Whoa, this looks way too complex to be something to just lead you astray. I shouldn't even be looking at this stuff. Take it to Trias--he'll be able to make sense of it. And DON'T let anyone get in your way. This is bigger than me. It might even be bigger than him, but we'll see.\nAnd do me a favor, ‹name›, don't tell anyone I helped you. If my superiors found out I knew about any of this and didn't share it with them they'd probably hang me.","rew":"Experience: 250","back":"I see you're back, and in one piece. We both know you're not here for cheese, so let's cut out the pleasantries. Was Backus any help, or have you even left for Duskwood yet?","done":"Yeah... this is an interesting read. Jorgen and DeLavey were smart to bring me in on this.\nSeems the Defias have been trying pretty hard to complete this plan of theirs. Hmm... what's this? Fist? That's a familiar name.\nDuskwood Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":74.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Watcher Backus","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"605":{"id":605,"t":"Singing Blue Shards","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Singing Crystal Shards to Crank Fizzlebub.\n10 Singing Crystal Shard Stone Maw Basilisk 80 % , Crystal Spine Basilisk 80 % , Cold Eye Basilisk 80 % , Thrashtail Basilisk 80 % and 1 more","desc":"The Singing Crystals are unique to Stranglethorn, and are very valuable to certain parties. I can move those crystals, but the cursed Venture Company makes it hard for an honest entrepreneur like myself to gather any!\nI'd like to hire you.\nThe basilisks in Stranglethorn eat the crystal. This gives them their hardened skin, and sometimes decent quality crystal can be harvested from it.\nYou can get it from any basilisk, but the less nasty ones are along the shores south of Zul'Kunda, to the north.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Do you have those shards yet? I'll give you a decent cut from the profits!","done":"Aha! These will do nicely, ‹name›. Yes, quite nicely!\nHere is your cut, and...it was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.2,"n":"Crank Fizzlebub","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"205":{"id":205,"t":"Troll Witchery","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Skullsplitter Fetishes to Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp.\n4 Skullsplitter Fetish Skullsplitter Mystic 80 % , Skullsplitter Witch Doctor 80 %","desc":"While I study those legends you acquired, gather for me implements of evil troll magic. Enter the territory of the Skullsplitter trolls, a second tribe to the distant south, and acquire Skullsplitter Fetishes from their Witchdoctors and Mystics.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have those fetishes, ‹name›? They might hold the secret to Kurzen's degradation...I must know!","done":"Thank you. I will study these fetishes and see if they hold the secret of Kurzen's fall into evil.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":37.8,"y":3.6,"n":"Brother Nimetz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8365":{"id":8365,"t":"Pirate Hats Ahoy!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Haughty Modiste wants you to collect 20 Southsea Pirate Hats and return them to her at Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris.\n20 Southsea Pirate Hat Andre Firebeard 10 % , Southsea Swashbuckler 10 % , Southsea Dock Worker 10 % , Southsea Freebooter 10 % and 2 more","desc":"You're the help the Cartel sent? I suppose you'll do. Listen carefully ‹class›. As you know, I am a procurer of fashionable apparel for the elite of Azerothian society. Kings and Queens, Warchiefs and, well whatever the Horde calls their queens, all wear what I choose is in style. And they pay through the nose for it, which is the best part.\nSo here's what's going to happen. You head down to Lost Rigger Cove and acquire a lot of pirate hats by whatever means. Do you think you can handle that?","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Do you have all 20 hats? I don't believe you, let me see them. They better be in pristine condition!","done":"Oh you're a darling, even if it did take you longer than I am accustomed to. This shipment should make me quite a bit of money once I've cleaned and personalized these hats. And seeing as I'm always willing to reward work that's well done, here's a little something for you. I suggest that you spend some of it on a bath sweetie.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":66.6,"y":22.3,"n":"Haughty Modiste","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2605":{"id":2605,"t":"The Thirsty Goblin","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect a Laden Dew Gland and bring it to Marin Noggenfogger in Gadgetzan.\nLaden Dew Gland Thistleshrub Dew Collector 10 %","desc":"I've got an idea, see. I've heard of some strange creatures called dew collectors that live to the southwest... and that they are able to store water in special glands.\nI think that if I could get one of these glands, I could create a drink that would quench my terrible thirst! Do you think you could help me, ‹name›?\nLook for the cactus garden, ‹name›; that's where you'll find the dew collectors.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Please, tell me you found the dew collectors?","done":"Oh, wonderful! Give it here -- let me drink it!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.8,"y":28.7,"n":"Marin Noggenfogger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8925":{"id":8925,"t":"A Portable Power Source","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Magma Lord Bokk in the Burning Steppes, obtain his Magma Core and bring it to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan.\nMagma Core Magma Lord Bokk","desc":"Next we shall need to find a stable and portable source of energy to keep the ectoplasm active. I've heard rumors of a mighty elemental called Magma Lord Bokk, whose heart is a powerful magma core - an endless supply of heat!\nIt's said he can be found in the Burning Steppes, south of Blackrock Mountain. Bring the magma core to me and we shall have enough juice to power the extra-dimensional ghost revealer!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you found the Magma Lord, ‹name›?","done":"You've done it! This will certainly provide enough energy to power up the extra-dimensional ghost revealer!\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8765":{"id":8765,"t":"The Changing of Paths - Invoker No More","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\n15 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n15 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n15 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","back":"Champion, should you decide to walk another path, present me with your signet ring and a mountain of scarabs from our enemies in Ahn'Qiraj.","done":"Be well, ‹name›. If you change your mind, I shall be here to assist you.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"6365":{"id":6365,"t":"Meats to Orgrimmar","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Zargh's Meats to Devrak in the Crossroads.\nZargh's Meats\nProvided: Zargh's Meats","desc":"I have some choice cuts of meat that I want to send to a friend. Her name is Gryshka, the innkeeper in Orgrimmar. Will you deliver the meat for me?\nThe fastest way to Orgrimmar is on a wind rider. Take the meats to the Crossroads wind rider master, Devrak, and speak with him about transport to Orgrimmar.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You need to get somewhere fast? Then you're talking to the right orc!","done":"You have to get this meat to Orgrimmar? That is no problem. For a small fee, my wind rider can take you there.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.6,"y":29.8,"n":"Zargh","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.3,"n":"Devrak","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"845":{"id":845,"t":"The Zhevra","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Zhevra Runners to collect 4 Zhevra Hooves for Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.\n4 Zhevra Hooves Zhevra Runner 80 % , Zhevra Charger 80 % , Zhevra Courser 80 % , Swiftmane 80 %","desc":"The zhevra, although not the fiercest beast in the Barrens, are a shade tougher than the plainstriders. Don't worry -- we'll send you against bigger prey in good time, but for now your teeth could use a little more cutting.\nHunt the zhevra to the north and south, and collect their hooves. Bring them to me and perhaps we'll next send you against something tougher.","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How many zhevra have you slain?","done":"Not bad, ‹name›. Those zhevra hold a lot of strength in their legs. A sharp kick from them can knock even a tauren on its haunches!\nIt looks like you have some strength in you too. Are you ready for a real challenge?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"97005":{"id":97005,"t":"Cholaruk the ravener","lv":21,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring Chol'aruk's Head to Bainham in the Barrens.\nChol'aruk's Head","desc":"There's rumors of a monstrous abomination that makes its lair at a cave to the northwest of here, on the plateau known as Thorn Hill. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or \"The Ravener\" and those that have seen it say its so massive that it can swallow an orc whole.\nFew believe such tales, but I do... because I've fought one like it myself. On the honor of those I lost to these things, this beast must die.\nGather strong allies and find the lair of Chol'aruk. Kill the abomination and bring me it's head.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nChol'aruk's Trophy Sword Big Bad Basher Quilboar Toothpick Thornwoven Shield\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,100\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"It took six of us to defeat one of these creatures, and it still managed to kill all but myself and one other before we were able to bring it down.\nThis far from alliance lands I should leave it well enough alone. Light knows I'll lose little sleep over a few tauren savages or orcish brutes. However, the honor of my fallen brothers demands action.","done":"My dead men will rest easier knowing that there is one less of these monsters in the world. You've done well, and are a true and stalwart defender of the alliance. Thank you.\nGo with honor, Gryma.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":61.8,"y":39.4,"n":"Bainham","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"97485":{"id":97485,"t":"Traditions of the bluff","lv":10,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Purchase a Bundle of Herbs from Nida the herbalist, a Bundle of Ceder Twigs from Nata the enchanting supplier, and Sinew Thread from Mahu the leatherworking supplier and Ceremonial Flint and Tinder from Naal the cooking supplier.\nCombine the items and sprinkle the incense off of Hunter's Rise.\nPrepared Incense\nSpread incense","desc":"Blessings of An'she, friend.\nWe tauren have a tradition of scattering incense to the winds and I was hoping you'd be interested in honoring this tradition.\nYou will need to craft the incense by purchasing herbs from Nida, cedar from Nata, sinew thread from Mahu in the mid rise, and ceremonial flint and tinder from Naal on the upper rise. Once you have these items, combine them and spread them off the south facing cliff of Hunter's Rise.\nYou will find a mat and incense at the ceremonial site.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Prepared Incense\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"There are many occasions one may choose to spread incense to the winds. You could be asking the Earthmother to watch over someone, bless a hunt, celebrate an occasion, or even to seek guidance from our ancestors.\nOr it could be something else entirely.\nThough the act is done with reverence, it is not strictly a ceremonial affair. Typically there are certain traditional steps observed when performing this act, but many tribes have differing practices.","done":"You have done well.\nI thank you for taking the time to perform one of our time-honored traditions, ‹race›. I hope that as you travel you will find plenty of occasions you wish to give thanks for.\nShould you ever wish to perform the ritual again, you should be able to repurchase the components I sent you to collect.\nGo with An'she's warmth.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":38.2,"y":56.2,"n":"Eylah Sunhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"365":{"id":365,"t":"Fields of Grief","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Steal 10 pumpkins from the farm to the west, just north of Deathknell and take them to Apothecary Johaan in Brill.\n10 Tirisfal Pumpkin Tirisfal Pumpkin","desc":"What have we here? You look like a fledgling ‹class›. If you hope to prove yourself to The Dark Lady, you need to learn the ways of The Forsaken.\nTo the west you'll find a farm. Humans infest the land like mold on a rotting corpse. And worse yet, the Scarlet Crusade patrols nearby from their tower. Teach those scum a lesson and steal 10 of their precious pumpkins.\nOnce you have 10, take them to Apothecary Johaan in Brill.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Deathguard Simmer sent word that you were going to provide me with some much needed reagents. Were you able to gather 10 pumpkins yet, ‹name›?","done":"You have performed your bidding well, young ‹class›. You are proving yourself to be quite an asset to The Dark Lady's army.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":40.9,"y":54.2,"n":"Deathguard Simmer","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.4,"n":"Apothecary Johaan","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"445":{"id":445,"t":"Delivery to Silverpine Forest","lv":10,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Apothecary Johaan's findings to Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine Forest.\nJohaan's Findings\nProvided: Johaan's Findings","desc":"Time is a luxury that is not afforded to those of us under the employ of Lady Sylvanas. Surely you know this by now.\nAs a member of the Royal Apothecary Society it is my duty to share my knowledge with my colleagues so that our collective efforts might one day provide The Dark Lady with the New Plague she so badly desires.\nTake these findings to Apothecary Renferrel who is stationed at The Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Follow the roads to the south from Brill. From the Undercity go southwest.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"What business do you have with me, ‹class›?","done":"Ah, how good of Apothecary Johaan to send his research. With so many new developments here in Silverpine, I nearly forgot about the findings coming out of Lordaeron and Tirisfal Glades. Which reminds me, I need to get those samples off to the Necropolis soon.\nBut you must excuse my rambling. Extend your stay in Silverpine, ‹name›. We could use an able bodied ‹class› like you around here.\nTirisfal Glades Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.4,"n":"Apothecary Johaan","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4285":{"id":4285,"t":"The Northern Pylon","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Discover the location of the Northern Crystal Pylon in Un'Goro Crater.","desc":"What could they be for? I can't get the thought out of my head!\nIt's driving me crazy -- that the rumors I have heard about the crystal pylons are all true. Call me gullible, but I'll usually believe anything people tell me.\nAnyway, I have heard that there is one of the crystal pylons fairly close. Somewhere in the north... Please locate it, ‹name›. I just know they exist.","rew":"Experience: 3,950","back":"Have you visited the pylon, ‹name›?","done":"I know the stories are true, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1485":{"id":1485,"t":"Vile Familiars","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Vile Familiar Heads to Ruzan.\n6 Vile Familiar Head Vile Familiar 80 %","desc":"Those warlocks who came before us have earned the distrust of the Horde, and while we are tolerated, we are not loved.\nThis has not brought the warlocks closer together, however, as many choose to live reclusively, dabbling in their magics alone. I will not seek to lead you down one path or the other, but only help you in your maturation.\nBefore I teach you the art of summoning, bring me six heads of the vile familiars from the cave to the northeast.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Imp\nExperience: 360","back":"It is important that you can control the beings that you summon through your magic. There are few enough interested in learning the ways of the warlock that I would risk throwing your life away by teaching you something before you are ready.","done":"Throughout your training as a warlock, you will learn to call forth beings of many sorts. Some may not seem it, but all are useful tools.\nDo not be fooled by the imp's small size. As you no doubt noticed, it is still a formidable adversary.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.6,"y":69,"n":"Ruzan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1805":{"id":1805,"t":"Tome of the Cabal","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Reconstructed Tome and 3 Rods of Channeling to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.\nReconstructed Tome\n3 Rod of Channeling Dragonmaw Bonewarder 80 % , Dragonmaw Shadowwarder 80 %\nProvided: Reconstructed Tome","desc":"This is one of the most interesting texts I have perused in the last few years. The selection here is sparse--mostly books on geography--and I have already read them all. I should hope that Strahad would send me a copy of this tome when he has the chance.\nSpeaking of him, he sent word to me while you were away. For your task, you must obtain three rods of channeling.\nFor allowing me to look at this text, I will share a secret: You can find the rods on orcs of the Dragonmaw Clan in the Wetlands.","rew":"Experience: 2,450","back":"Yes, ‹name›? Of what service can I be to you?","done":"Well done! The Tome of the Cabal and three pristine--slightly scratched, I suppose--rods of channeling.\nThis will be interesting. It's been some time since a young warlock took on a felhunter to make his own.\nUndercity The Barrens Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":75.9,"y":37.9,"n":"Jorah Annison","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5405":{"id":5405,"t":"Argent Dawn Commission","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Commission\nExperience: 550\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission. Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer.\nWhile under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess. Procure these insignia and bring them to me. For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token.\nAchieve your destiny, ‹class› join the fight today!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.2,"y":68.4,"n":"Argent Officer Garush","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"6285":{"id":6285,"t":"Return to Lewis","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a gryphon ride to Sentinel Hill from the gryphon master Dungar Longdrink, then take Osric's Crate to Lewis at Sentinel Hill.\nOsric's Crate\nProvided: Osric's Crate","desc":"The gryphon master in Westfall is Thor. If you've spoken to him before, then you can take one of my gryphons to him.\nThat's a good lesson to know: gryphons are always trained to fly to their capital city, but they'll only take you to a remote gryphon master after you've already been there.\nYou've already been to Thor, so just speak with me again when you're ready to take a gryphon to Westfall. Once there, you can deliver Osric's Crate to Quartermaster Lewis.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You're back from Stormwind? Did Osric send the armor?","done":"Great, you brought the armor! We'll get this divvied to those who need it immediately.\nThank you, ‹name›. Your efforts have been a great help to us. And now that you're no stranger to gryphons, I hope you'll come and lend your aid to Sentinel Hill often!\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":71,"y":72.5,"n":"Dungar Longdrink","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":57,"y":47.2,"n":"Quartermaster Lewis","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"285":{"id":285,"t":"Search More Hovels","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Continue searching the Murloc hovels for the Menethil Statuette.","desc":"This grouping of Murloc hovels, after a thorough inspection, reveals nothing.\n...but you're certain that the next clue you find will be fruitful.\nOne of the hovels to the north must have the Menethil Statuette!","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"This barrel is halfway buried amidst the mud and grass ...","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":13.6,"y":38.2,"n":"Sealed Barrel","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":13.9,"y":34.8,"n":"Half-buried Barrel","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"6605":{"id":6605,"t":"A Strange One","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 550 experience instead of 650, 0.85 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Winna Hazzard in Felwood.","desc":"I just got back from Felwood, ‹name›. On my way through, I stopped at Bloodvenom Post and I met a very odd character... She seemed intent on one thing, and I suppose I could tell you what that is, but I think she'd like to explain it to you herself.\nIf you're interested, head to Bloodvenom Post in western Felwood and look for Winna Hazzard.\nWho knows, she might need your help...","rew":"Experience: 550\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"Ah, ‹class›. I see that there is hope yet. Are you here to assist me?\nWinterspring Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.1,"y":38.4,"n":"Harlo Wigglesworth","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":34.2,"y":52.3,"n":"Winna Hazzard","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5085":{"id":5085,"t":"Mystery Goo","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report back to Donova Snowden with your findings.\nFlask of Mystery Goo\nProvided: Flask of Mystery Goo","desc":"The greenish substance inside the cauldron appears to be similar to what you found in the flask. This strange gooey stuff could be as corrupted as the furbolg that created it...\nIf the Winterfall furbolg are using it, does this mean that they will soon be as corrupted as the Deadwood tribe?\nIt would be best to report back to Donova with your findings, along with a sample of the liquid in the cauldron.","rew":"Experience: 4,350\n+75 reputation with Everlook","back":"I hope you found something, ‹name›. The Winterfall are becoming increasingly aggressive!","done":"You are very resourceful, ‹name›. Do you think that the Winterfall furbolgs have been to the Deadwood camp?\nFelwood Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":60.2,"y":5.8,"n":"Deadwood Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5245":{"id":5245,"t":"Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use Jaron's Pick to find the four Highborne Relic Fragments. Bring them to Aurora Skycaller in Eastern Plaguelands.\nFirst Relic Fragment Highborne Relic Fragment\nSecond Relic Fragment Highborne Relic Fragment\nThird Relic Fragment Highborne Relic Fragment\nFourth Relic Fragment Highborne Relic Fragment\nProvided: Jaron's Pick","desc":"The highborne spirits are miserable creatures, that's for sure. They are still searching for pieces of the very thing that has cursed them to Kel'Theril forever -- the stolen relic.\nIf you are that interested, take my pick and go south to the lake, see if you can gather the pieces of it from within the ice.\nNow, I can't tell you a thing about what you find, but I do know of someone who might... Aurora Skycaller; she dwells near the Northpass Tower in the northern part of Eastern Plaguelands.","rew":"Experience: 5,800\n+25 reputation with Alliance","back":"Why have you come here?","done":"The past of the high elves is something that I do not wish to discuss, ‹name›. Please, it pains me to think of all that has happened... And that there is no way to make things right.\nWinterspring Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":52.1,"y":30.4,"n":"Jaron Stoneshaper","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":46.5,"y":16,"n":"Aurora Skycaller","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92685":{"id":92685,"t":"The hills have eyes","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Loot 7 Blood-Stained Bandit Masks from Highwayman Bandits in the Gustberry Lowlands.\n7 Blood-Stained Bandit Mask","desc":"The bandits have camps all over and there's a small one in the hills just north of here. Head up there and start cracking skulls. If we can catch them off guard and take them out before they come for us, we might just even the odds enough to stand a chance.\nBring me their masks. The bloodier the better.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Red Delicious Stormapple\nExperience: 775","back":"If you manage to bring me enough bandit masks, maybe I'll stitch a blanket out of them and give it to Ferauu.\n<Aamelia laughs loudly.>","done":"When I said the bloodier the better, you really listened. Good. It lets me know you made it hurt.\nOn a serious note, thank you for what you've done so far. I've been floating aimlessly around this farm for weeks as if I was just waiting for the end to come. I think I'm starting to have hope again.\nFerauu and his thugs are due any time now. All that's left is to go out and face them. What do you say, will you see this through to the end with me?","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93165":{"id":93165,"t":"Mercy falls on deaf ears","lv":13,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Al'Aketh Cultist's Ears from the Al'Aketh cultists in Shadowgale Forest, the Shine of Akir, or Gustberry Lowlands.\n10 Al'Aketh Cultist's Ear","desc":"The Al'Aketh have visited great tragedy upon our enclave, and blood must be repaid with blood.\nI have an offer for you, stranger. Should you find conflict with these accursed cultists, bring me the ears of those you kill. I will reward you for each that you return with in both coin and, in time, access to the Nightclaw's secrets should you prove yourself to be a true friend.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nNightclaw Gloves Shadowgale Pants Cult Hunter's Boots\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+1,000 reputation with Nightclaw Druids","back":"I will not rest until my fangs have gone through the throat of every single cultist on this isle.","done":"Excellent work. Only good things can happen by eliminating the cult. Hopefully this sends a message that the Nightclaw are not to be trifled with and that our resentments run deep.\nI suspect you have your work cut out for yourself, taking on the cult. If you gather more ears bring them here.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":63.8,"y":36,"n":"Vayn Moongaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8045":{"id":8045,"t":"The Heathen's Brand","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nHeathen's Brand\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","done":"Know this, heathen: A catastrophe has brought us together. Your pagan ways are neither understood nor appreciated by Zandalar but we are a fair people. Wear this brand around your neck. It shall serve as both a warning to our enemies and a symbol of your friendship to Zandalar.\nContinue to serve our people and I will amplify the power of the brand.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});